      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=[-2(a+b)]^2-4(4)(ab)\\\\\\Delta&=4(a+b)^2-16ab\\\\\\Delta&=4(a-b)^2\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nSince the discriminant is non-negative for all real $a,b$, the graph has at least one $x$-intercept.\n\nWhen $a=b$, $\\Delta=0$ and there is one $x$-intercept. When $a\\ne b$, $\\Delta>0$ and there are two.",
